        { id: "s17", label: "17. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s18", label: "18. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 企业合并 · The acquisition method for combinations not under common control, plus the distinctive common-control carve-out · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Two fundamentally different accounting models, depending on control history</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 20 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of BUSINESS COMBINATIONS — SPLIT into TWO fundamentally DIFFERENT categories DEPENDING on WHETHER the COMBINING entities were UNDER common CONTROL both BEFORE and AFTER the COMBINATION (see the COMPANION ASBE No. 2 poster for the PREDECESSOR-cost treatment) or NOT (WHERE the ACQUISITION method — CLOSELY converged with IFRS 3 — applies).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Two Categories of Business Combination</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Common control vs arm's-length acquisitions</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Measurement approach</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Under common control</span><span>PREDECESSOR cost (CARRYING amount) method — NO goodwill RECOGNISED (see the COMPANION ASBE No. 2 poster)</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Not under common control</span><span>ACQUISITION method — FAIR value MEASUREMENT, GOODWILL (or BARGAIN purchase GAIN) recognised</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Acquisition Method — Combinations Not Under Common Control</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Identifying the acquirer, measuring net assets at fair value</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR combinations NOT under COMMON control, the ACQUISITION method APPLIES — IDENTIFYING the ACQUIRER, DETERMINING the ACQUISITION date, and RECOGNISING the IDENTIFIABLE assets ACQUIRED, liabilities ASSUMED, and any NON-CONTROLLING interest at FAIR VALUE at the ACQUISITION date — CONSISTENT with IFRS 3's OWN acquisition method internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Measuring and Recognising Goodwill</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Consideration transferred plus NCI, less net identifiable assets</div><div class="text-supporting">GOODWILL is MEASURED as the EXCESS of (a) the CONSIDERATION transferred PLUS the AMOUNT of any NON-CONTROLLING interest, OVER (b) the FAIR value of the ACQUIREE'S identifiable NET assets ACQUIRED — CONSISTENT with IFRS 3's OWN goodwill CALCULATION internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Goodwill — Impairment-Only, Genuinely Aligned With IFRS 3</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">No systematic amortisation — a point of genuine international alignment</div><div class="text-supporting">GOODWILL recognised UNDER this Standard is MEASURED at COST LESS accumulated IMPAIRMENT losses (see the COMPANION ASBE No. 8 poster) — WITH NO systematic AMORTISATION, TESTED for IMPAIRMENT AT LEAST annually — CONSISTENT with the IMPAIRMENT-only approach applied UNDER IFRS 3/IAS 36 internationally. This is a GENUINE point of ALIGNMENT with IFRS, in CONTRAST to Japan GAAP'S mandatory GOODWILL amortisation requirement (see the COMPANION ASBJ Statement No. 21 poster EARLIER in this SERIES).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Negative Goodwill (Bargain Purchase Gain)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognised immediately, after reassessment</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the FAIR value of the ACQUIREE'S net IDENTIFIABLE assets EXCEEDS the CONSIDERATION transferred (a "BARGAIN purchase"), the ACQUIRER first RE-ASSESSES whether it has CORRECTLY identified ALL assets ACQUIRED and LIABILITIES assumed, and CORRECTLY measured THEIR fair VALUES — WITH any REMAINING excess recognised IMMEDIATELY as a GAIN in PROFIT or LOSS, CONSISTENT with IFRS 3's OWN treatment internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Acquisition-Related Costs — Expensed as Incurred</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Not capitalised into the cost of the combination</div><div class="text-supporting">COSTS the ACQUIRER incurs in CONNECTION with a BUSINESS combination (LEGAL fees, DUE diligence COSTS, advisory FEES) are EXPENSED as INCURRED — EXCEPT costs of ISSUING debt or EQUITY securities, WHICH are accounted FOR under THEIR own RESPECTIVE standards — CONSISTENT with IFRS 3'S own treatment internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Step Acquisitions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Remeasuring a previously held interest to fair value</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE an ACQUIRER already HELD an EQUITY interest in the ACQUIREE BEFORE obtaining CONTROL (a "STEP acquisition"), the PREVIOUSLY held INTEREST is REMEASURED to FAIR value at the ACQUISITION date, WITH the RESULTING difference RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS — CONSISTENT with IFRS 3'S own step-acquisition TREATMENT internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Common Control Combinations — Recap and the Restatement Practice</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Comparative financial statements often restated as if combined from the start</div><div class="text-supporting">AS discussed in the COMPANION ASBE No. 2 poster, COMBINATIONS UNDER common CONTROL use a PREDECESSOR-cost method, WITH NO goodwill RECOGNISED. A GENUINELY distinctive ADDITIONAL feature of THIS treatment: COMPARATIVE financial STATEMENTS are OFTEN RESTATED as IF the COMBINATION had OCCURRED from the BEGINNING of the EARLIEST period PRESENTED (an "AS-IF pooling" restatement APPROACH) — a PRACTICE without a DIRECT parallel under IFRS 3, WHICH has NO equivalent common-CONTROL exception REQUIRING comparable RESTATEMENT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>The Measurement Period</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Retrospective adjustments within a limited window</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the INITIAL accounting for a BUSINESS combination is INCOMPLETE by the END of the REPORTING period in WHICH the combination OCCURS, PROVISIONAL amounts are USED, WITH retrospective ADJUSTMENTS permitted WITHIN a SPECIFIED "measurement PERIOD" following the ACQUISITION date — CONSISTENT with IFRS 3's OWN measurement period CONCEPT internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising Goodwill in an Arm's-Length Acquisition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The standard goodwill calculation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An acquisition of an unrelated company</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquires 100% of an unrelated target for RMB 600,000,000 cash. The target's identifiable net assets have a fair value of RMB 480,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">GOODWILL = RMB 600,000,000 − RMB 480,000,000 = <strong>RMB 120,000,000</strong>, recognised on the BALANCE Sheet, SUBJECT to ANNUAL impairment TESTING, with NO systematic AMORTISATION.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Worked Example — a Bargain Purchase Gain</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognising a gain rather than goodwill</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An acquisition below the target's net asset fair value</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquires 100% of a distressed but fundamentally sound target for RMB 200,000,000. After reassessment, the target's identifiable net assets have a fair value of RMB 235,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a BARGAIN purchase GAIN of RMB 235,000,000 − RMB 200,000,000 = <strong>RMB 35,000,000</strong>, recognised IMMEDIATELY in PROFIT or LOSS.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 20 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Name and description of the acquiree, acquisition date, and consideration transferred</span><span>Amounts recognised for identifiable assets acquired, liabilities assumed, and goodwill (or bargain purchase gain)</span><span>Whether the combination was under common control, and the measurement basis applied</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a combination is genuinely under common control</span><span>Identifying the acquirer in a combination</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of identifiable assets acquired and liabilities assumed</span><span>Fair value of any non-controlling interest and previously held equity interest</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 3</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 20 vs IFRS 3</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 20</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 3</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Acquisition method (arm's-length combinations)</span><span>Same framework</span><span>Same framework — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Common control combinations</span><span>Predecessor cost, no goodwill, often restated comparatives</span><span>NO exception — acquisition method applies regardless</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Goodwill subsequent treatment</span><span>Impairment-only</span><span>Impairment-only — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">FOR arm's-length COMBINATIONS, this is a GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — the COMMON-control EXCEPTION remains the SINGLE most SIGNIFICANT, well-KNOWN divergence, as DISCUSSED in the COMPANION ASBE No. 2 poster.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every business combination event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Goodwill recognition (arm's-length)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Subject to annual impairment testing</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Bargain purchase gain</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised immediately</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 2</span><span>Long-term Equity Investments — supplies the common-control combination measurement approach this Standard incorporates</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 8</span><span>Impairment of Assets — governs the annual goodwill impairment testing this Standard requires</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s18"><span class="num">18</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Bargain purchase gain</div><div class="glossary-def">A gain recognised where the fair value of an acquiree's identifiable net assets exceeds the consideration transferred, after reassessment.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Measurement period</div><div class="glossary-def">The window following an acquisition date during which provisional business combination accounting may be retrospectively adjusted as new information emerges.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe20 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
